1
00:00:00,043 --> 00:00:00,084
.

2
00:00:24,943 --> 00:00:27,779
<i>Die Bergkatze</i> was restored in 2000
by the Friedrich Wilhelm Murnau Foundation.

3
00:00:27,904 --> 00:00:30,615
The basis was a camera negative
from the Bundesarchiv-Filmarchiv, Berlin.

4
00:00:30,740 --> 00:00:32,408
The intertitles contained in the negative

5
00:00:32,534 --> 00:00:34,577
do not correspond to
the wording of the censor-card,

6
00:00:34,702 --> 00:00:36,162
and they were in bad condition.

7
00:00:36,287 --> 00:00:38,915
The wording of the reconstructed intertitles
is based on the censor-card.

8
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:41,376
The copying was carried out
by L'lmmagine Ritrovata in Bologna.

9
00:00:41,501 --> 00:00:44,546
The master negative of this reconstruction
was used in 2014 for the 2K digital version.

10
00:00:44,837 --> 00:00:48,508
<i>THE MOUNTAIN-LION/ THE WILDCAT</i>

11
00:00:48,633 --> 00:00:53,137
A Grotesque in 4 Acts
by Hanns Kräly and Ernst Lubitsch

12
00:00:53,263 --> 00:00:54,597
Direction: Ernst Lubitsch

13
00:00:54,722 --> 00:00:56,933
Sets and Costumes: Ernst Stern

14
00:00:57,058 --> 00:00:58,518
Cinematography: Theodor Sparkuhl

15
00:00:58,643 --> 00:01:01,062
CAST:

16
00:01:01,187 --> 00:01:04,357
The Fortress Commander: Viktor Janson
His Wife: Marga Köhler

17
00:01:04,482 --> 00:01:07,652
Their Daughter: Edith Meller
Lieutenant Alexis: Paul Heidemann

18
00:01:07,777 --> 00:01:10,905
Claudius, Leader of a Band of Robbers:
Wilhelm Diegelmann

19
00:01:11,030 --> 00:01:12,699
Rischka, His Daughter: Pola Negri

20
00:01:12,824 --> 00:01:15,827
Pepo, a Shy Robber: Hermann Thimig

21
00:01:15,952 --> 00:01:19,122
Dafko: Paul Biensfeld
Zofano: Paul Grätz

22
00:01:19,247 --> 00:01:23,293
Masilio: Max Kronert
Tripo: Erwin Kopp

23
00:01:23,418 --> 00:01:27,297
Setting for the action:
not far from Piffkaneiro

24
00:01:27,422 --> 00:01:30,466
FIRST ACT.

25
00:04:12,837 --> 00:04:15,631
Quiet!

26
00:04:50,082 --> 00:04:53,544
Lilli, daughter of the commander.

27
00:06:27,430 --> 00:06:33,102
<i>To the Commander</i>
<i>of the Border Fortress!</i>

28
00:06:33,227 --> 00:06:39,442
<i>Lieutenant ALEXIS has been sent</i>
<i>to your unit as punishment. By decree.</i>

29
00:06:39,567 --> 00:06:47,199
<i>Lieutenant Alexis, who is known</i>
<i>by all the women here as "Dashing Alex",</i>

30
00:06:47,325 --> 00:06:50,786
<i>is to be treated firmly.</i>

31
00:06:50,912 --> 00:06:55,499
<i>- General of Not-Far-from-Piffkaneiro</i>

32
00:06:58,044 --> 00:07:01,172
At last, a dashing man.

33
00:07:31,661 --> 00:07:34,914
What a swine!

34
00:07:37,208 --> 00:07:40,586
That's how you talk about Alexis?

35
00:07:43,673 --> 00:07:46,968
Alexis leaves the residence.

36
00:08:44,567 --> 00:08:47,445
Sweetheart!

37
00:09:17,808 --> 00:09:21,020
A word of send-off. -

38
00:09:24,315 --> 00:09:29,695
The heart breaks, tears well up.
Yearning stings, tonsils swell up...

39
00:09:38,537 --> 00:09:42,792
So take your leave in peace.
You have been good to all of us.

40
00:09:49,423 --> 00:09:52,593
I did what I could.

41
00:10:14,323 --> 00:10:17,868
Adieu! Daddy!

42
00:10:40,975 --> 00:10:45,521
Robber-leader Claudius and his men,
the terror of the border.

43
00:10:51,694 --> 00:10:54,530
Good morning, men!

44
00:10:57,116 --> 00:11:00,536
Good morning, leader sir.

45
00:11:09,211 --> 00:11:12,047
Unload!

46
00:11:25,019 --> 00:11:28,439
Well, what have you stolen?

47
00:11:33,736 --> 00:11:37,198
Where have you been all this time?

48
00:11:39,742 --> 00:11:42,453
I was in Kientopp.

49
00:12:06,685 --> 00:12:09,688
Not on the back of the head

50
00:12:12,233 --> 00:12:15,361
Rischka, my child.

51
00:13:10,291 --> 00:13:13,627
She hit me.

52
00:13:16,797 --> 00:13:19,550
Me too.

53
00:13:44,616 --> 00:13:47,494
Don't spoil them

54
00:14:18,317 --> 00:14:21,195
Towel.

55
00:17:50,862 --> 00:17:53,824
Ah, look here.

56
00:18:23,478 --> 00:18:26,523
Drop your trousers.

57
00:19:10,484 --> 00:19:14,071
Ah, look here.

58
00:19:49,731 --> 00:19:52,859
As you do to me, so I do to you.

59
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:04,162
END OF THE FIRST ACT.

60
00:20:04,663 --> 00:20:08,041
SECOND ACT.

61
00:20:49,791 --> 00:20:53,128
The robbers!

62
00:20:59,760 --> 00:21:03,346
...have waylaid the lieutenant.

63
00:21:19,362 --> 00:21:22,115
Speak!

64
00:21:47,098 --> 00:21:50,352
Out of nowhere, a gunshot!

65
00:22:04,533 --> 00:22:07,869
Now I've had enough of this!

66
00:22:21,758 --> 00:22:24,636
Find Lieutenant Alexis right away!

67
00:22:44,906 --> 00:22:47,701
You see, I am he...

68
00:23:39,961 --> 00:23:42,756
The lieutenant.

69
00:24:09,282 --> 00:24:12,327
But what delightful drawers.

70
00:25:09,009 --> 00:25:13,430
Excuse me,
I shall introduce you to my wife!

71
00:25:17,058 --> 00:25:20,186
My dear maiden daughter.

72
00:25:25,734 --> 00:25:29,237
You like my maiden daughter - no?

73
00:25:48,089 --> 00:25:51,843
It won't be so easy
to win my daughter as your wife.

74
00:27:50,670 --> 00:27:54,132
That can't be.

75
00:29:41,322 --> 00:29:44,701
Why did you let him run away?

76
00:29:49,539 --> 00:29:53,918
...and those lovely drawers;
I could have used a pair.

77
00:30:05,263 --> 00:30:08,182
You would have split them though.

78
00:30:13,771 --> 00:30:17,108
You have no idea how cold I am.

79
00:30:19,569 --> 00:30:22,780
The punitive expedition
against the robbers.

80
00:31:48,116 --> 00:31:51,536
Go make some coffee in the meantime.

81
00:32:08,386 --> 00:32:11,389
Children, show some pizzazz!

82
00:32:18,271 --> 00:32:21,274
If you please, maestro.

83
00:32:41,002 --> 00:32:43,921
They're shooting.

84
00:33:19,332 --> 00:33:22,293
Don't get rough.

85
00:33:23,836 --> 00:33:26,797
War is war.

86
00:34:10,383 --> 00:34:14,762
We're not going to allow ourselves
to take a thrashing.

87
00:34:46,919 --> 00:34:49,964
Hi there!

88
00:35:03,060 --> 00:35:06,522
That lass has spirit.

89
00:35:11,027 --> 00:35:14,822
END OF THE SECOND ACT.

90
00:35:15,323 --> 00:35:20,161
THIRD ACT.

91
00:35:46,312 --> 00:35:50,691
A decisive victory.

92
00:37:21,782 --> 00:37:27,872
You went to town on them
like Hector on the steak!

93
00:37:43,554 --> 00:37:46,974
It is to you that we owe
this wonderful victory.

94
00:37:59,945 --> 00:38:03,407
As thanks, you shall receive
my daughter's hand.

95
00:38:06,285 --> 00:38:09,830
I can't possibly ask that of you.

96
00:38:11,791 --> 00:38:15,002
Indeed - you can ask that of me.

97
00:38:33,145 --> 00:38:35,940
Then there's nothing to be done.

98
00:39:42,798 --> 00:39:45,759
The victory celebration.

99
00:47:53,914 --> 00:47:57,334
I've never smelt so good!

100
00:49:35,307 --> 00:49:37,851
Occupied!

101
00:49:42,981 --> 00:49:46,359
Shame on you - in my wardrobe.

102
00:50:13,720 --> 00:50:17,140
Soon we'll be married.

103
00:50:19,726 --> 00:50:23,063
That's what I'm afraid of.

104
00:55:51,891 --> 00:55:55,311
There's nothing to be done -
I'll have to have you arrested.

105
00:56:37,478 --> 00:56:40,815
Out with you, you impertinent being.

106
00:56:55,747 --> 00:56:58,541
Trouble afoot.

107
00:57:44,796 --> 00:57:48,174
Ten legs - five men -
that's about right.

108
00:58:04,315 --> 00:58:07,777
END OF THE THIRD ACT.

109
00:58:08,319 --> 00:58:11,531
FOURTH ACT.

110
00:58:11,656 --> 00:58:15,159
Rischka is dreaming.

111
00:59:01,164 --> 00:59:04,709
Do you hear my heart aflutter?

112
01:02:11,479 --> 01:02:15,024
This is the time of golden love.

113
01:02:28,996 --> 01:02:32,166
The girl has to get married.

114
01:02:46,138 --> 01:02:50,434
You promised her to one of us!

115
01:02:53,604 --> 01:02:57,316
What I've promised, I'll stick to!

116
01:03:08,411 --> 01:03:11,747
You have to get married!

117
01:03:14,542 --> 01:03:17,962
Don't talk so dirty!

118
01:03:38,190 --> 01:03:41,569
Who'd like to marry me?

119
01:03:56,917 --> 01:03:59,837
I would!

120
01:05:03,526 --> 01:05:06,612
Rischka's wedding day.

121
01:06:21,395 --> 01:06:24,940
Do you want to make
my daughter happy?

122
01:06:57,389 --> 01:07:07,388
<i>Always be loyal and honest,</i>
<i>until your chilly grave</i>

123
01:07:53,821 --> 01:08:00,452
<i>Following the young couple's</i>
<i>official wedding yesterday,</i>

124
01:08:00,578 --> 01:08:06,667
<i>today the betrothal</i>
<i>of Lieutenant Alexis</i>

125
01:08:06,792 --> 01:08:11,797
<i>to the daughter of our fortress</i>
<i>commander will be celebrated.</i>

126
01:11:09,558 --> 01:11:13,020
Lieutenant, we must be off
to the wedding celebration.

127
01:14:44,731 --> 01:14:48,151
That would seem to suit you.

128
01:15:48,795 --> 01:15:52,215
I want to go get a little more comfortable!

129
01:17:01,368 --> 01:17:04,913
Why did you give him our child?

130
01:18:42,761 --> 01:18:46,139
He loves you more than me!

131
01:18:52,479 --> 01:18:56,900
I'll cure him of that,
as much as it pains me!

132
01:22:24,274 --> 01:22:27,902
What took you so long?

